{%- doc -%}
  Echoes the Klaviyo sign-up form id for the shopper's current language.

  Klaviyo has no multi-language forms — each language is its own form, addressed
  by id. Klaviyo's own "show on certain URLs" targeting does not help here either,
  because `openForm` opens a form directly and bypasses targeting, so the id has
  to be chosen per locale on this side.

  Matched on the language part of the locale, so regional variants (pt-PT, pt-BR,
  es-ES, es-MX) all resolve to the same form. Anything unmapped falls back to the
  English form. To add a language, add a `when` with its Klaviyo form id.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign kl_lang = request.locale.iso_code | downcase | split: '-' | first

  case kl_lang
    when 'pt'
      echo 'Ycf8mL'
    when 'es'
      echo 'UDZBxF'
    else
      echo 'XGSauY'
  endcase
-%}
